## Evolve assistant: suggest the intent and the fix, grounded in Genie Pages

Context: Typing the typed intent by hand was the main friction, and business
words ("VOR", "the GERMANY market") only make sense with the organisation's
glossary. The assistant reads the ontology and the Genie Pages selected on
the version, then suggests; coverage, validation and evaluation still decide.

Changes:
1. src/agents/agent_ontology_evolution/
   Two read-only tool loops (intent, proposal), one validated submit each, one repair.
2. src/back/objects/ontology/evolution/{ContextPages,IntentValidator,EvolutionAssistant}.py
   Pages from the version allowlist, read as the caller; a quote is kept only if it is in the page; an uncited path hint is dropped.
3. src/back/objects/ontology/evolution/ProposalBuilder.py
   The model picks a profiled join and names it; SQL is still built from checked columns.
4. src/api/routers/internal/evolution.py, UI
   `POST /evolution/intent/suggest`; `source: "agent"` on proposals.
5. tests/eval
   Glossary dataset with and without pages, injection page, live runner.

Modified files:
- see the PR file list

Tests: uv run --frozen pytest -q tests/units/ontology/evolution → 231 passed
